msgid ""
"Since the https://quarkus.io/blog/ja-quarkus-io/[launch] of Japanese https://"
"ja.quarkus.io[ja.quarkus.io], we got contributors translating the website "
"into (simplified) Chinese at https://cn.quarkus.io[cn.quarkus.io] and "
"recently we added Spanish at https://es.quarkus.io[es.quarkus.io] too."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"These sites are now accessible via the drop-down \"globe\" menu in the top-"
"right corner."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"I find it amazing and want to thank the ~30 contributors who have helped to "
"translate the website into these languages and continues to do so!"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Especially big thanks to Yoshikazu Nojima for creating the first "
"infrastructure to handle ja.quarkus.io translations using a mix of computer "
"aided translation and human edit/verification. Big thanks for Zheng Feng and "
"Ruben Novelli to reuse this setup for for cn.quarkus.io and es.quarkus.io "
"respectivelly."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you want to help improve the language coverage see the readme file in one "
"of the following repositories:"
msgstr ""

msgid "https://github.com/quarkusio/ja.quarkus.io for Japanese"
msgstr ""

msgid "https://github.com/quarkusio/cn.quarkus.io for Chinese (simplified)"
msgstr ""

msgid "https://github.com/quarkusio/es.quarkus.io) for Spanish"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Or if you want to create a translation for a new language, copy one of the "
"above repositories and check out the README for more details."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If questions post at https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"discussions[discussions] and mention `@maxandersen` ."
msgstr ""

msgid "Have fun!"
msgstr ""
